//? Title: Soundex: actual consonant classes and deliberate collisions
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A name index should retrieve some spelling variants under a common coarse key.
American Soundex retains the first letter and encodes later consonant classes
into three digits, deliberately losing distinctions. We trace actual branches,
retain the original twenty surnames, and separate transparent H/W from vowel
resets.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Map BFPV to1, CGJKQSXZ to2, DT to3, L to4, MN to5 and R to6. Retain the first
uppercase byte and initialize the previous class from it. Emit a consonant class
only when it differs from the previous class. Vowels/Y reset the previous class,
while H/W leave it unchanged. Stop at three digits and pad with zeros.

For Ashcraft, S and C share class2 and H is transparent, so the C is suppressed.
A vowel between equal classes instead permits both. The trace contains the
actual consumed prefix, each class decision and the final padding step. A suffix
after the key is full is not processed, although the complete byte policy still
checks it.

The map is intentionally many-to-one. Equal keys can help candidate retrieval
but do not prove equal pronunciation or identity, and different keys can miss
plausible variants. Initial letters are retained, so Catherine and Katherine do
not collide despite sounding alike in some accents. There is no universal
guarantee of catching all spelling variants.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/soundex_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/soundex.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::soundex_trace("Ashcraft");
    std::print("| actual offset | uppercase | class | previous | actual branch | actual partial key |\n| " "---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.history)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.offset,
                   s.action == "pad" ? "(pad)" : std::string(1, s.uppercase),
                   s.group, s.previous, s.action, s.partial);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Name Ashcraft; H is transparent");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual consumed bytes", r.scanned_bytes));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual key {}", r.code));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/soundex_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual offset | uppercase | class | previous | actual branch | actual partial key |
| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | A | 0 | 0 | retain-first | `A` |
| 1 | S | 2 | 0 | append | `A2` |
| 2 | H | 0 | 2 | transparent | `A2` |
| 3 | C | 2 | 2 | suppress | `A2` |
| 4 | R | 6 | 2 | append | `A26` |
| 5 | A | 0 | 6 | reset | `A26` |
| 6 | F | 1 | 0 | append | `A261` |
| 7 | (pad) | 0 | 1 | pad | `A261` |
\image(figures/soundex_tiny.svg)
// result_end
