> API and interpretation

ASCII names are case-insensitive and locale-independent. No letter filtering is
performed: legacy punctuation/digit behavior retains the first byte and treats
later uncoded bytes as resets. Non-ASCII bytes are preserved rather than
transliterated; the linguistic rules are specified only for ASCII names. The old
report mentioned a4000-word jellyfish check without retaining its corpus or
receipt; it is not asserted as fresh evidence here. The original twenty-name
cohort remains fully reproducible.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

